The plan in .agents/plans/M7.md is approved with these corrections:
1. Write scripts/spike_voice_asr.py FIRST and print "SPIKE READY" in your output when it compiles, then continue. I run it
   outside your sandbox while you build; you reconcile in a later job. Build voice.py against provisional fixtures and
   a fake upstream as planned.
2. Licence and keystore are the owner's decisions: write LICENSE only if the owner confirms (leave a TODO line in
   README "Licence: TBD by owner" for now and do NOT add a LICENSE file); the release script and docs/RELEASE.md as
   planned, no keystore creation.
3. Two judge-visible fixes from the live site to include in §2:
   a. SAM returned 3 masks for the concept "battery"; only one is the battery (the others are black plastic boxes).
      Show each mask's confidence on the overlay, highlight the highest-confidence mask as the match and draw the rest
      faint and labelled "other candidates", in web and the report. No change to recorded data.
   b. Trace "Meaning" text reads "...no fault showing up makes this more likely — Unlikely (about 2 in 10)". Make it
      "...makes this more likely; now unlikely (about 2 in 10)" (direction of the update, then the new band), in
      levels.py so web and report agree; regenerate the demo bundles offline if their texts change (re-key the demo
      cache offline if needed, live outputs untouched) and keep make_demo_bundle.py --check green.
4. README: describe the build honestly and factually: Muse Code wrote the code from AGENTS.md/SPEC.md during the event,
   driven headlessly with plans and reviews on muse-wonder-1.0 and builds on muse-spark-1.3 (prompts and runs are in
   .agents/). Do not claim anything about who wrote the prompts.
Implement the plan in order, each step with its test before the next. Keep the full backend suite under 3 minutes. Run
the plan's verification commands except owner-run ones and `modal deploy` (backend via .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q;
Android offline with seeded GRADLE_USER_HOME; web npm ci --offline), fix failures until they pass, add a dated
docs/DECISIONS.md entry, and do not commit. Foreground commands only. Finish with files created/changed, test counts,
the acceptance sweep table, and pass/fail of each command.
